Subject: [PATCH] server: Map ACEs that match the current token to the Unix owner bits.

sd_to_mode() gave the user (and group) bits only for ACEs of the descriptor's owner SID,
and only when that owner was in the caller's token. Every file is owned on the Unix side
by the user running Wine, though, whatever SID the descriptor names as owner. When the
owner is a SID the token does not have, the current user's own "full control" ACE was
ignored and the folder lost its write bits:

 - prefixes first used with another Wine build: upstream Wine's user SID is
   S-1-5-21-0-0-0-1000, Proton's is derived from /etc/machine-id, so descriptors written
   earlier keep the old owner (also after moving a prefix to another machine);
 - descriptors whose owner was set to another SID (Administrators, SYSTEM, ...).

Adobe's installers and apps (adobe_caps.dll, HDPIM.dll) re-apply the DACL of
"Common Files\Adobe\caps" (Administrators: all, Everyone: read, plus the inherited ACEs)
with SetNamedSecurityInfo(). The folder became r-xr-xr-x, SQLite could not create its
journal next to hdpim.db, and every install stopped with "Error in setting package
install status ... Error code: 105" (Media Encoder 2020, Photoshop 2020). Wine also could
not store the new descriptor afterwards, since writing the xattr needs the write bit.

ACEs that match the token (user, enabled groups; deny-only groups for deny ACEs) now
set or clear the user and group bits regardless of the owner SID. Descriptors whose
owner is the current user map as before.

Applied to the Proton-CachyOS 11.0 build as a binary patch by lib/patch_runner.py
(two jne -> jmp after the owner check in sd_to_mode).
---
--- a/server/file.c	2026-10-02 17:46:38.406294309 +0300
+++ b/server/file.c	2026-10-02 17:46:47.585986478 +0300
@@ -610,8 +610,10 @@
                     {
                         bits_to_set &= ~((mode << 6) | (mode << 3) | mode); /* all */
                     }
-                    else if (token_sid_present( current->process->token, owner, TRUE ) &&
-                             token_sid_present( current->process->token, sid, TRUE ))
+                    /* The Unix owner of every file is the user running Wine, whatever SID the
+                     * descriptor names as owner (another Wine build, a moved prefix or a
+                     * SetNamedSecurityInfo() owner): ACEs that match our token set user bits. */
+                    else if (token_sid_present( current->process->token, sid, TRUE ))
                     {
                         bits_to_set &= ~((mode << 6) | (mode << 3));  /* user + group */
                     }
@@ -627,8 +629,7 @@
                         new_mode |= mode & bits_to_set;
                         bits_to_set &= ~mode;
                     }
-                    else if (token_sid_present( current->process->token, owner, FALSE ) &&
-                             token_sid_present( current->process->token, sid, FALSE ))
+                    else if (token_sid_present( current->process->token, sid, FALSE ))
                     {
                         mode = (mode << 6) | (mode << 3);  /* user + group */
                         new_mode |= mode & bits_to_set;
